  "findings": [
    "Message queue deduplication, not file scanner or image similarity; reject-domain remains. MIT read, no code adopted.",
    "compute_hash concatenates payload and context without length framing; distinct tuples payload ab/context c and payload a/context bc hash identical input bytes. Source-grounded ambiguity, no cryptographic collision claim.",
    "Hash excludes agent_id; embedded unit explicitly asserts equal payload across agents samehash. Scope isolation depends caller context pending protocol review.",
    "Cache TTL applies only memory; persistent fallback API has no timestamp parameter and repopulates now. Actual storage expiry pending storage source review.",
    "check_duplicate then record separate calls not atomic reservation; concurrent duplicate work possible, no race control executed. Wallclock now unwrap and u64TTL as i64 conversion unvalidated.",
    "Storage source resolves prior TTL question: write_dedup/check_dedup operate only in-memory DashMap with independent StorageConfig TTL. No persistent dedup backend IO despite comments; memory fallback may extend outer TTL until storageTTL expires.",
    "Storage payload_to_embedding repeats32B Blake3 digest across384dimensions; deterministic hash features, not learned semantic similarity. Test checks length only, no semantic relevance.",
    "Storage initialize discards collection-create errors; message cache insert precedes remote write and can survive failure. HTTP mutators do not check HTTP status. No remote requests executed; source review only.",
    "AiMessage new defaults dedup_context empty, so equal payload across agents share dedup key unless caller overrides. Validation does not include dedup context scoping; negative deadline accepted by validate positive-only check but is_expired flags it. NaN budget passes <=0 check; no runtime control yet.",
    "Protocol defines DeduplicationRecord timestamp nanoseconds/TTLmilliseconds, actual caches use seconds and separate tuple, no serialized record persistence in reviewed storage. Three files fully read after initial combined output truncation; storage/protocol reread complete."
